<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Mr. Bridger came in the same day after falling on his porch steps early this morning, three weeks after cataract surgery on his right eye. He says the right eye now sees sharply and brightly while the left is still blurred, and the two do not agree: the edge of the steps looked closer than it was, he missed the second step and put out his right hand to catch himself. He did not hit his head or his face, did not lose consciousness and got up by himself. His right wrist has been aching and swollen since, worse with gripping. He has no numbness in the hand. His right eye has no pain, redness or new blurring since the fall, and he is still putting in the steroid drops twice a day as the taper allows. He takes no blood thinners. He has used the diclofenac gel on his knees and put ice on the wrist. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Onset</td><td>This morning, falling forward on the porch steps onto an outstretched right hand</td></tr><tr><td>Location</td><td>Back and thumb side of the right wrist</td></tr><tr><td>Severity</td><td>5 out of 10, worse with gripping</td></tr><tr><td>Context</td><td>Three weeks after right cataract surgery; left eye still blurred; the two eyes see differently</td></tr><tr><td>Associated signs and symptoms</td><td>Swelling; no numbness, head strike, loss of consciousness, eye pain or new eye redness</td></tr><tr><td>Modifying factors</td><td>Ice and rest help</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.18"/>
    <code code="10187-3" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Review of systems Narrative - Reported"/>
    <title>Review of Systems</title>
    <text><table><thead><tr><th>System</th><th>Result</th><th>Finding</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Musculoskeletal</td><td>Positive</td><td>Right wrist pain and swelling; back and knees at their usual level</td></tr><tr><td>Eyes</td><td>Positive</td><td>Right eye clear; left eye blurred as before; the two images do not match; no eye pain, redness or flashes</td></tr><tr><td>Neurological</td><td>Negative</td><td>No head strike, headache, dizziness, loss of consciousness or numbness in the hand</td></tr><tr><td>Cardiovascular</td><td>Negative</td><td>No chest pain, palpitations or faintness before the fall</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>4 systems reviewed. [S]</paragraph></text>

  </section>
</component>

