<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="2.16.840.1.113883.10.20.22.2.9" extension="2014-06-09"/>
    <code code="51847-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Evaluation + Plan note"/>
    <title>Assessment and Plan</title>
    <text><list listType="ordered"><item><content styleCode="Bold">Right wrist sprain (S63.501A)</content>. A sprain of the right wrist from a fall on an outstretched hand. The X-ray with scaphoid views shows no fracture, and there is no snuffbox or scaphoid tenderness, so a hidden scaphoid fracture is unlikely; it will be re-examined at next week&apos;s visit. Hand nerves and circulation are normal. [S]<list><item>A removable wrist splint for comfort for one to two weeks, then gentle movement.</item><item>Ice for 15 minutes several times a day and elevation.</item><item>Diclofenac gel may be used on the wrist as on the knees, within the same daily maximum; acetaminophen up to 1 g three times a day if needed; no oral anti-inflammatories.</item><item>Return at once for increasing pain, numbness or a cold, pale hand; re-examine the scaphoid at next week&apos;s visit.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Fall risk between the two cataract operations (Z91.81)</content>. The fall came from the mismatch between a newly clear right eye and a still-blurred left eye, which upsets depth judgment on steps; this risk lasts until the second operation in three weeks. He did not strike the operated eye. [S]<list><item>Asked the eye surgeon&apos;s office about a temporary change to the right lens of his glasses to reduce the mismatch; they will fit it this week.</item><item>Second handrail and contrast tape on the porch steps now rather than later; a light on the steps at dawn and dusk.</item><item>No driving until after the second operation.</item><item>Keep the second operation as planned.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Cataract, after the right operation (H25.13)</content>. The right eye is quiet after the fall, with no sign of injury. [S]<list><item>Finish the right steroid drop taper as prescribed.</item><item>Call the eye surgeon the same day for eye pain, redness or blurring.</item></list></item></list><paragraph>Guideline basis: Cataract in the Adult Eye Preferred Practice Pattern (2021); Falls Prevention in Community-Dwelling Older Adults: Interventions (2024)</paragraph><paragraph>Follow-up: Wrist and falls review at the six-week visit, about a week from now, or sooner for the warning signs above. Second eye operation in three weeks. Next scheduled visit 1874-06-02: six-week review four weeks after right cataract surgery: vision, the drops, falls between operations, back pain and the wrist. [S]</paragraph></text>

  </section>
